"1rem" style="white-space: pre-wrap !important; overflow-wrap: normal !important; line-height: normal !important;  font-weight: 400 !important; font-style: normal !important; font-size: 1rem !important;">Ask about real behavior without leading someone.</li>
      <li data-template-id="target-two" class="canva-text" data-canva-font-size="1rem" style="white-space: pre-wrap !important; overflow-wrap: normal !important; line-height: normal !important;  font-weight: 400 !important; font-style: normal !important; font-size: 1rem !important;">Find patterns while preserving differences.</li>
      <li data-template-id="target-three" class="canva-text" data-canva-font-size="1rem" style="white-space: pre-wrap !important; overflow-wrap: normal !important; line-height: normal !important;  font-weight: 400 !important; font-style: normal !important; font-size: 1rem !important;">Justify a next decision with interview evidence.</li>
     </ul>
    </div>
   </aside>
   <section id="question" aria-labelledby="question-title" class="sheet p-5 md:p-8">
    <div class="flex gap-4 items-start">
     <span class="section-number">01 / BEGIN</span>
     <h2 id="question-title" data-template-id="question-title" class="canva-text display font-bold" data-canva-font-size="1.5rem" style="white-space: pre-wrap !important; overflow-wrap: normal !important; line-height: normal !important; color: rgb(36, 28, 48) !important; --canva-color: #241c30ff; caret-color: rgb(36, 28, 48) !important; font-family: 'DM Sans', sans-serif !important; font-weight: 700 !important; font-style: normal !important; font-size: 24px;">Question of the Day</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="rule my-5"></div>
    <div class="mb-5">
     <label for="student-name" data-template-id="student-name-label" class="canva-text field-label" data-canva-font-size="1rem" style="white-space: pre-wrap !important; overflow-wrap: normal !important; line-height: normal !important;  font-weight: 700 !important; font-style: normal !important; font-size: 1rem !important;">Student name</label> <input id="student-name" type="text" data-template-id="student-name-input" class="canva-input response short" data-export-label="Student name" autocomplete="name" placeholder="Enter your name" data-canva-font-size="1rem" style=" font-weight: 400 !important; font-style: normal !important; font-size: 1rem !important;">
    </div>
    <p data-template-id="question-prompt" class="canva-text leading-relaxed mb-5" data-canva-font-size="1rem" style="white-space: pre-wrap !important; overflow-wrap: normal !important; line-height: normal !important;  font-weight: 400 !important; font-style: normal !important; font-size: 1rem !important;">Which gives an entrepreneur stronger evidence: asking what someone says they would do, or asking what they actually did the last time? Explain.</p><label for="opening-answer" data-template-id="opening-label" class="canva-text field-label" data-canva-font-size="1rem" style="white-space: pre-wrap !important; overflow-wrap: normal !important; line-height: normal !important;  font-weight: 700 !important; font-style: normal !important; font-size: 1rem !important;">My first thought</label> <textarea id="opening-answer" class="response" data-export-label="Question of the Day"></textarea>
   </section>
   <section id="case" aria-labelledby="case-title" class="sheet p-5 md:p-8">
    <div class="flex gap-4 items-start">
     <span class="section-number">02 / READ</span>
     <h2 id="case-title" data-template-id="case-title" class="canva-text display font-bold" data-canva-font-size="1.5rem" style="white-space: pre-wrap !important; overflow-wrap: normal !important; line-height: normal !important; color: rgb(36, 28, 48) !important; --canva-color: #241c30ff; caret-color: rgb(36, 28, 48) !important; font-family: 'DM Sans', sans-serif !important; font-weight: 700 !important; font-style: normal !important; font-size: 24px;">The Calendly Case</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="rule my-5"></div>
    <p data-template-id="case-focus" class="canva-text italic text-[#625c69] mb-6" data-canva-font-size="1rem" style="white-space: pre-wrap !important; overflow-wrap: normal !important; line-height: normal !important; color: rgb(98, 92, 105) !important; --canva-color: #625c69ff; caret-color: rgb(98, 92, 105) !important;  font-weight: 400 !important; font-style: normal !important; font-size: 1rem !important;">Reading focus · Customer insight, questioning assumptions, and perseverance</p>
    <div class="reading max-w-4xl">
     <p><strong>The recurring frustration.</strong> Before founding Calendly, Tope Awotona worked in enterprise software sales. His work depended on conversations and meetings, but arranging those meetings often required repeated messages about available times. Time spent coordinating was time not spent on the purpose of the meeting.</p>
     <p><strong>The focused problem.</strong> Awotona founded Calendly in 2013 with a vision of simplifying scheduling and reducing the back-and-forth. A person could share availability so another person could choose a workable time. The insight: when finding time to meet is easier, useful connections can happen sooner.</p>
     <p><strong>The calculated commitment.</strong> Calendly’s official profile says Awotona invested his personal savings in the venture. That shows perseverance and calculated risk, but commitment alone does not prove customers need a product. A founder still needs evidence about who experiences a problem, how often it occurs, what people do now, and whether it matters enough to change behavior.</p>
     <p><strong>The customer evidence question.</strong> Awotona’s experience was a starting observation. Instead of “Would you use an easier scheduling tool?”, ask: <strong>“Tell me about the last time you tried to schedule a meeting with several people.”</strong> The second question invites a story about behavior, workarounds, delays, and priorities.</p>
     <p><strong>The continuing lesson.</strong> Calendly now serves individuals, teams, and organizations whose work depends on meetings. The lesson is not that every problem needs an app. Investigating a focused problem helps reveal what should be built, changed, or left alone.</p>
    </div>
    <p class="text-sm text-[#625c69] mb-6">Adapted for class from the NEIA Entrepreneur Hub Case 17 reading focus and <a href="#" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="underline text-[#61249a]">Calendly’s official company profile ↗</a>.</p>
    <div data-template-id="mark-panel" class="canva-panel bg-[#f6eefb] border-l-4 border-[#61249a] p-5 mb-7" style="background-image: linear-gradient(rgb(246, 238, 251), rgb(246, 238, 251)) !important; background-clip: border-box !important;">
     <h3 data-template-id="mark-title" class="canva-text font-bold mb-2" data-canva-font-size="1.1875rem" style="white-space: pre-wrap !important; overflow-wrap: normal !important; line-height: normal !important;  font-weight: 700 !important; font-style: normal !important; font-size: 19px;">Mark the Case as You Read</h3>
     <p data-template-id="mark-instructions" class="canva-text leading-relaxed" data-canva-font-size="1rem" style="white-space: pre-wrap !important; overflow-wrap: normal !important; line-height: normal !important;  font-weight: 400 !important; font-style: normal !important; font-size: 1rem !important;">Find the recurring problem, the founder’s starting observation, one assumption that still needs proof, and the stronger customer-discovery question.</p>
    </div>
    <h3 data-template-id="reflection-title" class="canva-text font-bold mb-5" data-canva-font-size="1.1875rem" style="white-space: pre-wrap !important; overflow-wrap: normal !important; line-height: normal !important;  font-weight: 700 !important; font-style: normal !important; font-size: 19px;">Case Reflection · Use Details from the Reading</h3>
    <div class="space-y-5">
     <div>
      <label for="case-one" data-template-id="case-one-label" class="canva-text field-label" data-canva-font-size="1rem" style="white-space: pre-wrap !important; overflow-wrap: normal !important; line-height: normal !important;  font-weight: 700 !important; font-style: normal !important; font-size: 1rem !important;">1. What problem did Awotona notice, and why might it matter to people whose work depends on meetings?</label><textarea id="case-one" class="response" data-export-label="Case reflection 1"></textarea>
     </div>
     <div>
      <label for="case-two" data-template-id="case-two-label" class="canva-text field-label" data-canva-font-size="1rem" style="white-space: pre-wrap !important; overflow-wrap: normal !important; line-height: normal !important;  font-weight: 700 !important; font-style: normal !important; font-size: 1rem !important;">2. Why is personal frustration useful but not enough to prove a solution should be built?</label><textarea id="case-two" class="response" data-export-label="Case reflection 2"></textarea>
     </div>
     <div>
      <label for="case-three" data-template-id="case-three-label" class="canva-text field-label" data-canva-font-size="1rem" style="white-space: pre-wrap !important; overflow-wrap: normal !important; line-height: normal !important;  font-weight: 700 !important; font-style: normal !important; font-size: 1rem !important;">3. What evidence would distinguish an occasional annoyance from a meaningful problem?</label><textarea id="case-three" class="response" data-export-label="Case reflection 3"></textarea>
     </div>
    </div>
   </section>
   <section id="lab" aria-labelledby="lab-title" class="sheet p-5 md:p-8">
    <div class="flex gap-4 items-start">
     <span class="section-number">03 / PRACTICE</span>
     <h2 id="lab-title" data-template-id="lab-title" class="canva-text display font-bold" data-canva-font-size="1.5rem" style="white-space: pre-wrap !important; overflow-wrap: normal !important; line-height: normal !important; color: rgb(36, 28, 48) !important; --canva-color: #241c30ff; caret-color: rgb(36, 28, 48) !important; font-family: 'DM Sans', sans-serif !important; font-weight: 700 !important; font-style: normal !important; font-size: 24px;">Question Lab</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="rule my-5"></div>
    <p data-template-id="lab-intro" class="canva-text leading-relaxed mb-6" data-canva-font-size="1rem" style="white-space: pre-wrap !important; overflow-wrap: normal !important; line-height: normal !important;  font-weight: 400 !important; font-style: normal !important; font-size: 1rem !important;">Strong questions ask about a specific past experience. They do not advertise an idea or pressure someone toward a preferred answer.</p>
    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-3 mb-6">
     <div class="small-card">
      <p data-template-id="weak-one" class="canva-text font-bold text-[#cc2474] mb-3" data-canva-font-size="1rem" style="white-space: pre-wrap !important; overflow-wrap: normal !important; line-height: normal !important; color: rgb(204, 36, 116) !important; --canva-color: #cc2474ff; caret-color: rgb(204, 36, 116) !important;  font-weight: 700 !important; font-style: normal !important; font-size: 1rem !important;">“Would you use an app that makes group work easier?”</p>
      <p data-template-id="strong-one" class="canva-text" data-canva-font-size="1rem" style="white-space: pre-wrap !important; overflow-wrap: normal !important; line-height: normal !important;  font-weight: 400 !important; font-style: normal !important; font-size: 1rem !important;">Try: “Tell me about the last group project you completed.”</p>
     </div>
     <div class="small-card">
      <p data-template-id="weak-two" class="canva-text font-bold text-[#cc2474] mb-3" data-canva-font-size="1rem" style="white-space: pre-wrap !important; overflow-wrap: normal !important; line-height: normal !important; color: rgb(204, 36, 116) !important; --canva-color: #cc2474ff; caret-color: rgb(204, 36, 116) !important;  font-weight: 700 !important; font-style: normal !important; font-size: 1rem !importa